// A LEVEL OF THE INFINITY FAMILY THAT IS NOT BUILT, AND NOTHING RUNS BEFORE IT
// (SATELLITE_INFINITY.md). check.sh asserts both.
//
// REBASED AT INF-2 (2026-09-19), and the rebase is the point. At INF-1 this file
// declared `satellite.variable.infinity my_inf = satellite.infinity()`, which INF-2
// built -- the line started working, exactly as this comment said it would. The
// vehicle is now a LETTERED LEVEL, the spec's own INF-6 example: there is no word
// for it at all yet (Part 5: "There are no rows for power, sat or any lettered
// level"), so the lexer reads `satellite.variable` and the checker says it is not a
// call.
//
// INF-6 BUILDS THIS -- the lexer pattern and the level token after each spelling --
// and then this goes red again. The fix is the same one: move it to whatever is
// still unbuilt (Part 11's `infinity-infinity`, which waits for Q16), never delete it.
satellite.include(satellite)

satellite.capsule satellite.main()
{
    satellite.console.display("before")
    satellite.variable.aasat my_aasat = satellite.aasat()
    satellite.return(satellite)
}
